Experiment-1.1(LeetCode problem 217)

Aim:- Given an integer array nums, return true if any value appears at least twice in the array, and return false if every element is distinct.

Algorithm:-
Initialize an empty hash set seen.
Iterate through each element num in nums:
If num already exists in seen, return True.
Otherwise, insert num into seen.
Return False if the loop finishes without finding duplicates.

Code:
class Solution:
    def containsDuplicate(self, nums: List[int]) -> bool:
        nums.sort()
        for i in range(1,len(nums)):
            if nums[i]==nums[i-1]:
                return True
        return False


Experiment-1.2(LeetCode Problem 219)

Aim:-Given an integer array nums and an integer k, return true if there are two distinct indices i and j in the array such that nums[i] == nums[j] and abs(i - j) <= k.

Alogorithm:-
Create an empty dictionary num to store each element and its latest index.
Traverse the array nums from index 0 to n-1.
For each element nums[i]:
Check if the element already exists in the dictionary.
If it exists, calculate the distance between the current index and the previously stored index.
If the distance is less than or equal to k, return True.
Update the dictionary by storing the current index of the element:
num[nums[i]] = i
Continue until all elements are processed.
If no valid duplicate is found, return False.

Code:
class Solution:
    def containsNearbyDuplicate(self, nums: List[int], k: int) -> bool:
        num={}
        for i in range(0,len(nums)):
            if nums[i] in num and abs(i-num[nums[i]])<=k:
                return True
            num[nums[i]]=i
        return False
